     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">a) 3 PLJ data innovations introduced to Bappenas, Ministry of Foreign Affairs, West Java Provincial Government

b) 1 of PLJ innovations adopted by West Java Provincial Government adopted the interactive map

c) Multiple numbers of contribution to awareness building, capacity, and ecosystem in data innovation in the Asia Pacific region:
  1.	Participating in FGD about data innovation in National Statistics led by UNFPA and UNRC Cambodia
  2.	For more awareness building please refer to: https://pulselabjakarta.org/search/media_coverage

d) Requests for collaborations, nationally and internationally: Ministry of Education and Culture Indonesia, Ministry of Finance Indonesia, UN Resident Coordinator Cambodia, UN Women, Price Waterhouse Cooper, Palladium, UNOPS, Facebook Data for Good, International Development Research Center (IDRC), The Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organization (CSIRO), Empatika Consultindo Mandiri

e) 6 technical inputs, nationally and internationally, provided: FGD with UNFPA regional and UNRC Cambodia, input on baselining methodology for PT Kereta Api Indonesia and Bappenas, input for Ministry of Foreign Affairs on how to develop and operate a sustainable digital dashboard, technical input for KOPERNIK on community air quality monitoring, technical input on the usage of conventional dan unconventional datasets to West Java Provincial Government, input on positive deviance method in agriculture to GIZ Data Lab Germany.

f) 3 academic papers/presentation published or presented at national and international conferences by PLJ:
  1.	The paper about resilience in Cambodia using microfinance accepted in the Machine Learning for Developing World (ML4D) workshop and presented in NeuRIPS conference.
  2.	PLJ&#x2019;s works in transportation modelling presented in Asia Pacific Transport Forum 2020, organized by ADB.
  3.	PLJ&#x2019;s MIND platform presented in Australasian Aid Conference in Cranford School of Public Policy, Australia National University, Canberra.

g) 80 public servants trained in data analytics: 50 Tim Analitika training within Bappenas Pusdatin, 10 public servants in JDS West Java and 10 public servants in Kemenlu 

h) At least 7 new partnerships in data innovation for development and humanitarian work (including the private sector): Facebook Data for Good, International Development Research Center (IDRC), The Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organization (CSIRO), PT Kereta Api Indonesia, Empatika Consultindo, UN Women and Gojek, Palladium.</narrative>
